(Title) Tj
T*
(TERM-HYP: Determining Optimal Delivery Timing in Hypertensive Pregnancy--A Multi-Center) Tj
T*
(Randomized Protocol) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Abstract) Tj
T*
(Hypertensive disorders of pregnancy complicate approximately 7% of gestations. Women who) Tj
T*
(maintain stable blood pressure control and reach term face a clinical decision regarding) Tj
T*
(delivery timing: immediate induction or expectant management pending spontaneous labor.) Tj
T*
(Early planned delivery may mitigate maternal hypertensive crises and adverse events but) Tj
T*
(carries potential for increased neonatal complications. This protocol describes a) Tj
T*
(50-center pragmatic randomized trial comparing two delivery strategies in women with well-) Tj
T*
(controlled hypertension at term. Eligible participants are those randomized at 36-37 weeks) Tj
T*
(gestation with singleton pregnancies. The intervention arm undergoes planned induction at) Tj
T*
(38 weeks; the comparator arm receives standard obstetric care. Co-primary outcomes address) Tj
T*
(both maternal and neonatal safety; secondary outcomes include cesarean rates and cost-) Tj
T*
(effectiveness. Follow-up extends to 6 weeks postpartum.) Tj
ET
